{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And who [is like Me].</b> And who will say that he is like Me:" "<b>יקרא.</b> <small>(as if to say)</small> Let him raise his voice:" "<b>ויגיד.</b> All that is coming, and let him set them before Me:" "<b>From the setting of [an everlasting people].</b> The first people, and the meaning of עולם is in time that has passed:" "<b>And the things.</b> A complete action, and that are to come, let him declare to their soul that they knew them:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {4 "'Things' translates אותיות (letters/things); 'complete action' translates פעל שלם, likely a grammatical term; the passage is compressed and textually uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:56.264099706Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}